        {
          "id": "bf93e16e-5c22-3d0a-80a3-da97257641cc",
          "content": {
            "id": "bf93e16e-5c22-3d0a-80a3-da97257641cc",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Netflix taps bank to explore bid for Warner Bros: sources",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Netflix is actively exploring a bid for Warner Bros Discovery's studio and streaming business.</p><p>Three sources told Reuters that Netflix has brought in investment bank Moelis & Co to explore the deal.\u00a0</p><p>That\u2019s the same firm that helped Skydance Media in its successful bid for Paramount Global.</p><p>The streaming giant has also been given access to Warner Bros Discovery\u2019s financial data, a key step in evaluating a potential offer.</p><p>Warner Bros and Moelis declined to comment, while Netflix could not be reached for comment.</p><p>Owning the studio business would give Netflix control over some of Hollywood's most successful stories and characters, including the Harry Potter and DC Comics franchises.\u00a0</p><p>:: File</p><p>Last week, Netflix CEO Ted Sarandos told investors the company evaluates acquisitions that could strengthen its content, but he said the firm had no interest in Warner Bros Discovery\u2019s cable networks.</p><p>Warner Bros has received multiple unsolicited offers to buy the company.</p><p>Its board is also weighing whether to proceed with a planned split or consider selling all or parts of the business.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Netflix is actively exploring a bid for Warner Bros Discovery's studio and streaming business.</p><p>Three sources told Reuters that Netflix has brought in investment bank Moelis & Co to explore the deal.&nbsp;</p><p>That\u2019s the same firm that helped Skydance Media in its successful bid for Paramount Global.</p><p>The streaming giant has also been given access to Warner Bros Discovery\u2019s financial data, a key step in evaluating a potential offer.</p><p>Warner Bros and Moelis declined to comment, while Netflix could not be reached for comment.</p><p>Owning the studio business would give Netflix control over some of Hollywood's most successful stories and characters, including the Harry Potter and DC Comics franchises.&nbsp;</p><p>:: File</p><p>Last week, Netflix CEO Ted Sarandos told investors the company evaluates acquisitions that could strengthen its content, but he said the firm had no interest in Warner Bros Discovery\u2019s cable networks.</p><p>Warner Bros has received multiple unsolicited offers to buy the company.</p><p>Its board is also weighing whether to proceed with a planned split or consider selling all or parts of the business.</p></body>",
